Chapter: TabServe
  cites Works chapter Http
  cites Works chapter WebRoute

 One HTTP request served inside a browser tab, for Prism's in-tab server
 demo. The page runs the module once per request: the raw request bytes are
 stdin and the encoded response is stdout. The route function is the one an
 app hands `web-serve` or `hosted-serve`, dispatched through the same
 `web-dispatch`, so the standard endpoints answer here too.

 WASM ONLY. `read-file-raw ""` reads stdin to end of input on that target,
 and the `+ 4` is its Text layout, a four-byte length before the bytes, the
 same reading `PlugBytes` makes.

 We say:

Section: Serve One Request

  ts-buf-to-list : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ts-buf-to-list (buf) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ts-buf-to-list buf (i + 1) n (list-push acc (peek-byte buf i))

  tab-serve-one : (HttpRequest -> HttpResponse) -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  tab-serve-one (route) = act
    raw <- read-file-raw ""
    let req = http-parse-request (ts-buf-to-list ((address-of raw) + 4) 0 (text-length raw) [])
    in let resp = if req.valid then web-dispatch route web-observe-none web-new req else http-error "Bad request"
    in write-binary (http-encode resp)
  end
